      "reproduction": [
        "Construct two immutable Commands with the same ID and metadata, with payload values True versus 1, or 1 versus 1.0. Assert their Command.digest() values differ.",
        "Supply both Commands to Projection.pending_command_ids with one valid command.received Event whose request_digest matches the LAST Command.",
        "Original dataclass equality treats the Commands as equal, silently overwrites the earlier identity and returns its pending ID rather than failing closed. Original four-test reviewer probe produced two assertion failures, no errors, exit 1."
      ],
      "impact": "Breaks the new pure pending projection fail-closed identity contract for conflicting canonical contents. SQLite primary-key reads do not themselves generate duplicate rows, so this is not evidence of an existing M0-04 store/idempotency regression or normal partial Handler commit.",
      "normative_basis": [
        "Design section 14.1: immutable Command and same-scope canonical idempotency content; section 13.10: recovery is based on durable facts.",
        "M0-05 approved boundary: contradictory persisted Command/receipt identity must fail closed. Existing Command.to_json()/digest() and Projection Event duplicate handling already use canonical serialization."
      ],
      "correction": "Use existing Command.to_json() for duplicate comparison. No digest format migration, input-ID omission, new command/schema or Handler change.",
      "closure_evidence": [
        "reviewer-identity-delta-hashes.log",
        "reviewer-identity-rerun.log",
        "reviewer-identity-regressions.log",
        "reviewer-identity-negative-control.log",
        "reviewer-corrected-focused.log"
      ],
      "closure_reason": "Same four independent probes now pass. Both new typed regressions and canonical-content positive control pass. Restoring old comparison solely in a disposable child process yields the two intended assertion failures with zero errors; positive control still passes. Current focused 38/38 and all eight hashes verified."
    }
